{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost blender ghost","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender GHOST Windowing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender GHOST C API","Blender GHOST Platform Class","Blender Main Event Loop","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender ghost blender ghost","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST.md","fileName":"Blender GHOST.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender GHOST","heading":"Blender GHOST","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"GHOST, the Generic Handy Operating System Toolkit, is Blender's internally maintained platform layer. It supplies windows, timers, cursors, clipboard and path services, input state, operating-system events, display settings, and the rendering contexts needed by the application.\n\nCore Blender calls the portable [[Blender GHOST C API]] rather than X11, Win32, or Cocoa directly. GHOST then selects a [[Blender GHOST Platform Class]] and wraps native details, allowing the [[Blender Main Event Loop]] and Blender window manager to remain largely independent of the host operating system.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender GHOST Windowing","Blender GHOST C API","Blender GHOST Platform Class","Blender Main Event Loop","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender GHOST.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Ful